{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfmza3JG9vZhbMm3EmPXb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I approved two of the seven rows (LLR-309 and TC-326) and sent the other five back, so the batch outcome is `OUTCOME: RETURN rows=7`. The verdict, the follow-up work and the approval are each committed.\n\n**Commits:**\n- **Verdict** (`38514de6`, trailer `WI: WI-841`): `docs/reviews/wi-841-done-when-blessed-in-lane/002-ADJUDICATE-be1e431.md`. The same commit adds a `## Dispositions` section to WI-841's spec with two drafts for intake to mint at merge.\n- **Approval** (`de1b1cde`): only those two rows' `Status` changed from Drafted to Approved, with the snapshot taken over both registries in the same commit. It is recorded as act seq 45 (`approved = [\"LLR-309\", \"TC-326\"]`) with no refusal, and its pre-commit checks passed. The five returned rows stay Drafted inside the copy.\n\n**Approved:**\n- **LLR-309:** it states SR-156's three hold points (build dispatch, hand close, merge) and their exemptions, and matches how they are wired. Two things it says are not yet checked by any test: that a review session is never held, and that the merge refusal names the digest. Those go back with TC-325.\n- **TC-326:** its tests check exactly what it claims, at all three hold points.\n\n**Returned:**\n- **LLR-307:** the most serious finding. If the claimed Done-when copy can't be read, nothing holds: not the build dispatch, the hand close or the merge, and the merge-time adjudication row isn't minted either. The adjudication brief, meanwhile, refuses that same unreadable claim, so nothing can release the lane through the normal path. The row gives no reason for failing open, and no test covers this case. It also writes the digest as bare hex, while verdicts must carry `sha256:<16 hex>`.\n- **LLR-308:** it holds two decisions. The done-when brief belongs under SR-156, but no requirement anywhere asks for the combined sitting.\n- **TC-325:** its Expected and Method leave out the merge-time hold, even though its own test checks it. \"The stated exemptions\" names no list, and nothing tests that a review session is exempt.\n- **TC-327:** it follows LLR-308's split. Its Expected can't be checked by observation, and several of LLR-308's refusals are untested.\n- **TC-328:** its Expected says a changed Done-when becomes \"either\" a successor draft \"or\" a new adjudication row. That is false for its own covered-change test, which mints neither. It also leaves out the refusal its Method runs.\n\n**Follow-up drafts:**\n1. Make the hold refuse when the claim can't be read, fix how LLR-307 writes the digest, and complete TC-325.\n2. Split LLR-308, trace the combined sitting to a requirement that asks for it (or label it as a derived requirement), and fix TC-327 and TC-328.\n\nI didn't run the test suite. Approving blesses the text only."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":814,"cache_read_input_tokens":161413,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":814},"output_tokens":745,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d1b1f362-046f-49c9-82c2-d234d9725442","uuid":"3b5e3332-2602-412d-a91d-9d7dd51fd5b7","timestamp":"2026-10-07T01:16:40.423Z","request_id":"req_011Cfmza2YcfXUAYubJVS8Eb"}
